 $('#rules').innerHTML=`<p class=mb-1><b>Semester GWA</b> = units-weighted average of that semester's valid subject records (Module 1). Lower GWA = better performance.</p><p class=mb-1><b>Trend:</b> a straight line is fitted through the semester GWAs (least squares). Slope below −${C.flat.toFixed(2)} per semester = <i>Improving</i> (GWA falling); above +${C.flat.toFixed(2)} = <i>Declining</i> (GWA rising); otherwise <i>Stable</i>. At least ${C.minTerms} semesters with records are required, otherwise <i>Insufficient Data</i> (no trend, forecast or flag).</p><p class=mb-1><b>Forecast:</b> the same line extended one semester past the latest semester with records, rounded to 2 decimals and kept within ${C.scaleMin.toFixed(2)}–${C.scaleMax.toFixed(2)}. It is an estimate, not a guaranteed result.</p><p class=mb-0><b>May need academic support</b> (supportive flag, not a judgement): trend is Declining; or latest GWA is worse than ${C.watchGwa.toFixed(2)}; or a ${C.failGrade.toFixed(2)} grade was recorded in the latest semester. These flag levels are monitoring aids set in the system, not university policy. Students with insufficient data are listed separately and never flagged.</p>`;
